(1968873, 270502, 44490, '<td valign="top">Interesting contrast, tree, and fence line, but I think that cropping more would be better.  Meeting the challenge is somewhat of a stretch.</td>', 'Interesting contrast, tree, and fence line, but I think that cropping more would be better.  Meeting the challenge is somewhat of a stretch.', '2005-12-21 17:27:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968877, 271368, 44490, '<td valign="top">Did you mean -  Doraphobia- Fear of fur or skins of animals?  Might also fit -  Ommetaphobia or Ommatophobia- Fear of eyes.  Cute photo, and a touch more DOF would be nice.</td>', 'Did you mean -  Doraphobia- Fear of fur or skins of animals?  Might also fit -  Ommetaphobia or Ommatophobia- Fear of eyes.  Cute photo, and a touch more DOF would be nice.', '2005-12-21 17:28:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968882, 271284, 44490, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea of juxtaposing auto and autophobia.  Better exposure of the person would help, and I think that the fence doesn''t help.</td>', 'Interesting idea of juxtaposing auto and autophobia.  Better exposure of the person would help, and I think that the fence doesn''t help.', '2005-12-21 17:30:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968886, 270247, 44490, '<td valign="top">Effective image and idea.  Would be better if something in the image were sharp.</td>', 'Effective image and idea.  Would be better if something in the image were sharp.', '2005-12-21 17:32:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968888, 270557, 47852, '<td valign="top">Since I can see the tailgate of the car in front of you, I''ll guess that the Chevrolet is the truck that is speeding, hence the title of your phobia.  However, the tailgate gets lost in the framing and bright lights.  My first reactions were that you should have cropped out the speedometer that shows your going at a slow speed for this one, and that  the driver should have been showing more fear in his expression captured in the mirror.</td>', 'Since I can see the tailgate of the car in front of you, I''ll guess that the Chevrolet is the truck that is speeding, hence the title of your phobia.  However, the tailgate gets lost in the framing and bright lights.  My first reactions were that you should have cropped out the speedometer that shows your going at a slow speed for this one, and that  the driver should have been showing more fear in his expression captured in the mirror.', '2005-12-21 17:33:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968915, 269583, 49513, '<td valign="top">i don''t think "phobia" when i see this photograph.  beautiful shot though.</td>', 'i don''t think "phobia" when i see this photograph.  beautiful shot though.', '2005-12-21 17:44:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968920, 271238, 44490, '<td valign="top">Scary - better sharpness / focus would help.</td>', 'Scary - better sharpness / focus would help.', '2005-12-21 17:46:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968923, 271062, 49513, '<td valign="top">way too much contrast</td>', 'way too much contrast', '2005-12-21 17:47:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968928, 269938, 44996, '<td valign="top">This image made me laugh. I just went to New Zealand, and I developed my 35mm prints by hand. I was so worried about light ruining the negative or not rolling it on correctly, or ect, ect. (they did turn out alright in the end, though) <br/>Technicaly, the image could have been a bit better. Perhaps a larger DoF to bring the rest of the negatives into focus. Good job other wise.</td>', 'This image made me laugh. I just went to New Zealand, and I developed my 35mm prints by hand. I was so worried about light ruining the negative or not rolling it on correctly, or ect, ect. (they did turn out alright in the end, though) Technicaly, the image could have been a bit better. Perhaps a larger DoF to bring the rest of the negatives into focus. Good job other wise.', '2005-12-21 17:48:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968941, 269449, 44996, '<td valign="top">I love the contrast, the framing of the building,  the sharpness of all the birds in motion, ect.   Good editing job to take acount for the quick shutter.  I bet somewill not vote as high because you simply didn''t show a person reacting to the birds, but it is one of my favorite for the challenge. Nice job.</td>', 'I love the contrast, the framing of the building,  the sharpness of all the birds in motion, ect.   Good editing job to take acount for the quick shutter.  I bet somewill not vote as high because you simply didn''t show a person reacting to the birds, but it is one of my favorite for the challenge. Nice job.', '2005-12-21 17:53:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968945, 270397, 44490, '<td valign="top">Love the position and capture of the mouse - it looks airborn, almost.  Would be better if the person were less central or more in focus.</td>', 'Love the position and capture of the mouse - it looks airborn, almost.  Would be better if the person were less central or more in focus.', '2005-12-21 17:54:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968952, 271350, 47852, '<td valign="top">Excellent use of lighting.  A great example of how to take something most would not fear and show the phobia side of it.  I think I might not have had him completely centered, and might have tried a few more shots to get him a bit more focused.  Overall though, a great job meeting the challenge!</td>', 'Excellent use of lighting.  A great example of how to take something most would not fear and show the phobia side of it.  I think I might not have had him completely centered, and might have tried a few more shots to get him a bit more focused.  Overall though, a great job meeting the challenge!', '2005-12-21 17:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968960, 270397, 47852, '<td valign="top">Cute mouse... great use of focus to emphasize the mouse... and excellent way to portray the scary phobia associated with the little guy by having the girl in the background, and with her broom no less!  Yep.. all around wonderfully done.  A 10! :)</td>', 'Cute mouse... great use of focus to emphasize the mouse... and excellent way to portray the scary phobia associated with the little guy by having the girl in the background, and with her broom no less!  Yep.. all around wonderfully done.  A 10! :)', '2005-12-21 17:58:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968967, 270953, 47852, '<td valign="top">A very dedicated model you have there to have put up with this.  I''m sure it wasn''t a quick pose with only one shot being taken.  Love the focus, the whites of her eyes pleading upward, and the outstretched hand.  A fantastic photo that met the challenge completely.  Nice job!</td>', 'A very dedicated model you have there to have put up with this.  I''m sure it wasn''t a quick pose with only one shot being taken.  Love the focus, the whites of her eyes pleading upward, and the outstretched hand.  A fantastic photo that met the challenge completely.  Nice job!', '2005-12-21 17:59:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968971, 270300, 47852, '<td valign="top">If Astraphobia is the fear of thunder and lightning, then this picture doesn''t make a lot of sense to me.</td>', 'If Astraphobia is the fear of thunder and lightning, then this picture doesn''t make a lot of sense to me.', '2005-12-21 18:02:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1968977, 271343, 16106, '<td valign="top">I would have liked to se more done with the lighting here, the sculpture is a bit flat  against such a white backround, and the centered straight ahead view point makes something pretty creepy, a bit too static.</td>', 'I would have liked to se more done with the lighting here, the sculpture is a bit flat  against such a white backround, and the centered straight ahead view point makes something pretty creepy, a bit too static.', '2005-12-21 18:04:42.000000', NULL, 1),
